--- B. ADAPT TIMING CLARIFICATION (microseconds, mean +/- SD) ---
   Adapt checked total       182.238 +/-  2.609   (PROTOCOL: las_adapt above, incl. internal PreVerify)
   witness-add only            5.648 +/-  0.032   (DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: z=z_hat+r'; not a protocol op)
   A real Adapt MUST pre-verify first; the witness-add line is a lower bound,
   not a usable operation.  Use 'Adapt checked total' for protocol cost.

--- C. COMMUNICATION (packed bytes; BYTE-LEVEL only, NOT EVM gas) ---
   public key    pk = t                2944
   secret key    sk = r                 512
   statement     Y = t'               2944   (63.4% of the signature; t' has pk size)
   witness       r'                    512   (same packed layout as sk = r)
   challenge     c_tilde                32   (H digest; FIPS 204 lambda/4 for this set)
   response      z (final)            4608   (99.3% of the signature)
   response      z_hat (pre-sig)      4608   (same packed layout as z)
   signature         (c, z)           4640
   pre-signature     (c, z_hat)       4640   (same size as the signature)
   final adapted sig (c, z)           4640   (an ordinary signature)
   commitment    w = A*y            internal computed commitment; hashed into c; not transmitted
   -- protocol-component catalogue (context; what each object is / why counted or not) --
   pp=(A,H)  A' seed                    32   (public params; only this 32-byte seed is transmitted)
   pp=(A,H)  expanded A'             11776   (n*ell polys; DERIVED from the seed, NOT transmitted)
   y (signing mask, S_gamma)         4608   (n+ell polys; INTERNAL, hashed into c via w, NOT transmitted)
   w = A*y (commitment)              2944   (n polys; INTERNAL, hashed into c, NOT transmitted)
   pi (NIZK well-formedness proof)    n/a   (paper-level off-chain proof; NOT implemented / NOT measured)
   tx metadata (addrs/amounts/nonces) excl   (application/ledger layer; EXCLUDED from this accounting)
   atomic-swap payload (byte-level only):
     off-chain   = Y + 2*pre-signature        =  12224   [= t' + 2*(c, z_hat)]
     settlement  = 2*signature                =   9280   [= 2*(c, z)]
     settlement incl. escrowed Y = Y + 2*sig  =  12224
   (EVM/keccak gas for on-chain verification is a separate axis; see evm/.)

--- D. COMPONENT MICROBENCHMARKS (microseconds, mean +/- SD) ---
   Cost-attribution ESTIMATES timing LOCAL COPIES of the inner steps
   (behaviourally identical to las.c) -- NOT the protocol entry points above.
   A-product / commitment w = A*y                         60.653 +/-  0.446
   challenge hash  c = H(pk, w(+t'), M)                   61.090 +/-  0.111
   NTT(s)  (n+ell polys; ONCE PER CALL, hoisted)          32.790 +/-  0.230
   NTT(c)  (one poly; once per attempt / per verify)       4.059 +/-  0.031
   c*r  (one poly; pointwise+invNTT, operands pre-NTT'd)   6.475 +/-  0.042
   c*r  per attempt (NTT(c) + n+ell pointwise+invNTT)     56.627 +/-  0.506
   norm check  |z|inf over n+ell polys                     2.498 +/-  0.048
   w + t'   (n polys)                                      5.509 +/-  0.020
   z_hat + witness r'   (n+ell polys)                      5.648 +/-  0.032
   c*t  per verify (NTT(c) + n x (NTT(t)+pw+invNTT))      46.771 +/-  0.483
   KeyGen/Gen: sample r (n+ell ternary polys)             13.175 +/-  1.373
     (KeyGen = sample r + A*r; A*r is the A-product line above; statement Y gen = KeyGen)
   Ext: s = z - z_hat   (n+ell polys)                      5.819 +/-  0.409
   Ext: A*s   (recompute statement; = an A-product)       59.505 +/-  0.277
   Ext: t' == A*s check   (n polys)                        0.575 +/-  0.012
   note: a full Sign/PreSign attempt applies c*r across N_PLUS_ELL = n+ell = 8
         response polynomials; Verify-style challenge multiplication applies
         c*t across LAS_N = n = 4 public-key polynomials.  NTT hoisting
         follows upstream ref/sign.c: NTT(s) is paid once per CALL (amortised
         over ~e rejection attempts), NTT(c) once per attempt / per verify.

--- E. NORM-MARGIN DIAGNOSTICS (achieved infinity-norm vs the reject bound;
       max over the 2000 sampled accepted signatures from section A) ---
   accepted |z|inf      max    122820   vs accept limit g-k   =    122820   (100.00% of band)
   accepted |z^|inf     max    122819   vs accept limit g-k-1 =    122819   (100.00% of band)
   Interpretation: the RESPONSE z/z^ saturates its band (~100%) -- the bound is
   the binding constraint and is exactly why ~63% of attempts are rejected.
   Contrast the AMHL cumulative WITNESS ||s_j||inf, which is tiny (<=K) vs the
   g-k-K band: that bound is extremely loose (see bench_app, the K-series table).
